com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress: withheld-oracle TDD is now GREEN in worktree /Users/joeoakhart/alm-85a5. RED coverage added for (1) no-op tick restarting a dead nginx-pinned MCP backend in place, (2) failed restart preserving identity/upstream and recording MCP backoff/deploy_failed, and (3) MCP_SELF_HEAL=0 kill switch restoring old log-only behavior. Implementation adds an in-place live-backend watchdog before no-op/source-change decisions, docker inspect port fallback for exited containers, health-contract wait, and existing deploy_failed/backoff reuse on failure. Focused validation: bash -n infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh and pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py both pass (58 tests). Next: lint/ratchets and full verify before commit/push.","timestamp":1788840671374191001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 2825 (commit 153a0ac7f544d6c3edc2e96421e269b59bfbecbb). Validation before push: focused pytest for the three withheld-oracle tests passed, full tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py passed (58 tests), make lint passed, and the required env-sanitized make verify passed on rerun. One earlier env-sanitized make verify run saw a single pytest failure, but an immediate env-sanitized pytest -m 'not integration and not external' -n 4 --dist worksteal -q -x rerun completed with exit 0, and the subsequent full make verify completed with exit 0. Awaiting Gerrit Verified +1 and LLM-Review +1 before submit/close.","timestamp":1788851373086518001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed Gerrit 2825 patch set 1 LLM-Review findings and pushed patch set 2 (commit 248eac6829607a26631783f11d490beb35bfaafa). Changes: self-heal now honors active MCP backoff before retrying; added RED/GREEN tests for post-restart health failure, active-backoff throttling, source-advancing deploy path ordering, and the docker inspect HostConfig.PortBindings fallback for exited containers. Validation after the fixes: bash -n infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh, full pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py (61 tests), make lint, and env-sanitized make verify all pass. Awaiting fresh Verified +1 and LLM-Review +1 for PS2.","timestamp":1788857432056179001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2825 submitted/merged at 2026-09-08 09:26:43 UTC after PS2 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments. Merged commit: 248eac6829607a26631783f11d490beb35bfaafa. No terraform/service restart was required: this is an autodeploy script change that will roll forward through the existing updater path.","timestamp":1788859626928674001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier remediation for non-codebase AC: the capacity/concurrency measurement citation lives in ticket evidence, not repo source. Concrete artifacts: enduring-ironclad-arrowana comment trail and Gerrit change 2807 document the retained plan-review snapshot reduction from 256,646,460 bytes to 37,046 bytes on a 9,081-ticket store, merged as 94c42343c1ba4546537e023f80d019ccfcd25014. The residual campaign inherited-americium-porpoise owns the remaining host capacity/off-box gate work rather than this serving-path self-heal. This ticket's design uses those measurements to reject blue/green self-heal because it would double MCP memory during pressure and instead chooses in-place restart under the existing serialized autodeploy flock.","timestamp":1788860407583642001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction follow-up: dropped enduring-ironclad-arrowana from my active assignment and read its merged Gerrit 2807 change first. That change trims long-lived plan-review relation snapshots to subject/direct child/prerequisite rows; it materially lowers retained review memory, but it does not touch autodeploy, nginx upstream selection, Docker restart behavior, or the failure mode where nginx remains pinned to an exited MCP backend. The barracuda reproduction therefore remains valid post-2807: tests simulate the residual serving-path fault directly (exited managed backend on nginx's live port) and prove it recovers via the merged in-place watchdog rather than persistent 502. Barracuda is already closed preexisting via Gerrit 2825.","timestamp":1788861447561267001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788753773815803001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"79b431f2-e058-4e7e-b4ec-ba3848660744","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"},{"link_uuid":"cbe3e2fe-ab92-4364-a329-188055694a26","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"},{"link_uuid":"7fbb59cf-d8cf-4305-b821-3c342f48ba55","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4d69-3853-924b-4949"},{"link_uuid":"2ba2aa46-fbbe-4ebf-9fd8-3b635e241903","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5e11-0d16-0314-45a5"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n/mcp can return persistent HTTP 502 after concurrent gate load if nginx's single-server upstream points at a dead MCP container. Parent witted-invisible-roan made autodeploy retain a crashed live backend instead of deleting it, but recovery can still wait for Docker/humans.\n\n## RCA / design decision\n\nRelated load-side ticket enduring-ironclad-arrowana already removed the biggest measured retained-memory multiplier: retained plan-review snapshot state fell from 256,646,460 bytes to 37,046 bytes on a 9,081-ticket store. This ticket fixes the serving-path residue.\n\nSelected prevention: an autodeploy in-place watchdog for the live MCP backend. On each serialized autodeploy tick (the existing flock owns check/start/readiness/backoff), MCP_SELF_HEAL defaults to 1 inside autodeploy.sh so the fix is active after merge; setting it to 0 is the kill switch. The watchdog uses the existing MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT readiness deadline. If MCP_SELF_HEAL=1 and the nginx upstream port maps to a managed MCP container that is not running, autodeploy runs docker start on the live container and readiness-checks that same port. A healthy running backend is a strict no-op. The port-to-container lookup must work for exited containers using inspect data, not docker port alone. Success leaves nginx byte-identical, clears MCP backoff, and logs recovery; failure leaves the container/upstream identity intact, emits existing AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-live-backend-down, records MCP backoff, and remains a retryable transient path; repeated backoff cycles are the operator escalation signal for a fatal start/config problem. Active MCP backoff is honored before retrying so repeated ticks do not hammer Docker. MCP_SELF_HEAL=0 disables the new branch and restores log-and-wait behavior.\n\nRejected alternatives: blue/green self-heal doubles MCP memory under pressure; nginx passive failover needs an already-live spare; Docker restart always is already present but is passive and not readiness/log evidenced; healthcheck watchdog/autoheal prior art supports this design and is implemented here through the existing autodeploy tick instead of a new daemon; instance sizing/off-box gates remain with inherited-americium-porpoise.\n\n## Testing / verification plan\n\n- RED/GREEN tests in tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py: no source change pending, nginx points at an exited managed MCP backend, one tick runs docker start for that exact container, upstream remains unchanged, success log appears, and readiness passes.\n- RED/GREEN tests for failure/kill switch/backoff: failed start or readiness does not remove the dead live backend, upstream remains unchanged, AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-live-backend-down and deploy_failed wiring appear, MCP backoff is recorded, active backoff skips restart, and MCP_SELF_HEAL=0 skips restart.\n- RED/GREEN tests for source-advancing ticks and exited-container port lookup: the watchdog runs before the ordinary blue/green deploy path, and the Docker stub only returns docker port for running containers so the docker inspect HostConfig.PortBindings fallback covers exited live containers.\n- Verified locally: bash -n infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh, pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py (61 tests), make lint, and env-sanitized make verify.\n- Live check after merge: no Terraform apply is required because failure visibility reuses existing deploy_errors wiring and success is operator-visible journald evidence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The selected design is recorded with why alternatives were accepted/rejected.\n- [x] A simulated MCP backend death recovers without persistent nginx 502.\n- [x] The prevention is covered by tests and visible through existing deploy-error alarm wiring plus logs.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Capacity/concurrency measurements cite enduring-ironclad-arrowana and the residual campaign inherited-americium-porpoise.\n  provenance: environment=rebar-ticket-store; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — cited ticket comments and Gerrit 2807 evidence are tracker/Gerrit artifacts, not repository source files.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"Add MCP live-backend self-heal path that replaces a dead nginx upstream backend without waiting for a source-changing deploy."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"Withheld-oracle tests for dead-live-backend self-heal and low-memory refusal."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"If needed, document the operator-visible self-heal marker and recovery semantics."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4d69-3853-924b-4949"],["relates_to","5e11-0d16-0314-45a5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1276942b-de4f-4ec5-be4c-512cc3410106","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"85a5-97ff-4a47-4c77","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent persistent MCP 502 recurrence","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f72291a2-338b-448f-a8b9-60892539296d","7fbb59cf-d8cf-4305-b821-3c342f48ba55","11c4e7f5-c096-495e-9ab8-9ade23391af0","2ba2aa46-fbbe-4ebf-9fd8-3b635e241903","eb732af1-37e5-4d0f-b306-f969f1344bca","33b1ff71-1de9-491d-bd5e-f26d04a218de","74cd25df-4651-4fd8-ad49-4715b2a0edb5","f6f0d6a3-34b7-4140-b351-fd8beefc5a8f","6c37d1ec-2674-4802-aa9c-7a188b58756c","1276942b-de4f-4ec5-be4c-512cc3410106","03485562-9a97-481a-92ab-a30e2b2423f6","c548494b-7ad1-4147-83fe-9da86f7af3f0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788870045114418001,"uuid":"a25d9697-51e6-4432-8683-7eb5267186b1"}